WEBVTT

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.241
in the last year of the travels

00:17:30.265 --> 00:17:32.983
are people who've had
something bad happen to them,

00:17:33.007 --> 00:17:36.517
and they turn that into
just a selflessness.

00:17:36.541 --> 00:17:38.638
And it's inspiring to be
around those people.

00:17:38.662 --> 00:17:40.330
I was in Englewood in Chicago.

00:17:40.354 --> 00:17:41.877
I was with a woman --

00:17:41.901 --> 00:17:45.022
and she lived in this neighborhood,
which is a tough neighborhood.

00:17:45.046 --> 00:17:48.118
And she decided she had to move out
because it was too dangerous.

00:17:48.142 --> 00:17:49.663
And the day she was moving out,

00:17:49.687 --> 00:17:52.401
she happened to see two girls
playing with broken bottles

00:17:52.425 --> 00:17:54.069
in an empty lot across the street.

00:17:54.093 --> 00:17:57.819
And she turned to her husband
and said, "We're not leaving.

00:17:57.843 --> 00:18:01.090
We're not going to be just another family
who abandoned this."